msgid "\\f[B]All Debian:\\f[R] Standard (xfce), Minimum (flux)\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:41
msgid "\\f[B]Bookworm/Trixie only:\\f[R] Toolbox, Ultra\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:43
msgid "\\f[B]Ubuntu:\\f[R] Standard only\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:46
msgid "\\f[B]Architectures:\\f[R] amd64, i386 (for older distributions)\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: minios-live.1:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: minios-live.1:47 minios-live.1:50 minios-live.1:97 condinapt.1:16
#: condinapt.1:18 condinapt.1:20 condinapt.1:22 condinapt.1:24 condinapt.1:26
#: condinapt.1:29 condinapt.1:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[bu]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:50
msgid ""
"It is advisable to use the latest version of Debian or Ubuntu for building."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:54
msgid ""
"\\f[B]WARNING\\f[R]: Never run scripts from the \\f[B]linux-live\\f[R] "
"folder directly.  It will break your system.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: minios-live.1:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:57
msgid ""
"\\f[B]minios-live\\f[R] breaks down the build process into discrete steps:"
"\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]build-bootstrap\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:60
msgid "Installs a minimal base system using \\f[B]debootstrap\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]build-chroot\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:64
msgid ""
"Installs the remaining core components and chosen desktop environment within "
"the chroot environment"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]build-live\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:67
msgid "Creates the main SquashFS image containing the core MiniOS system"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]build-modules\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:70
msgid "Builds additional SquashFS modules containing extra software packages"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]build-boot\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:74
msgid ""
"Copies the boot files, generates the initrd and the necessary boot "
"configuration files"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]build-config\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:77
msgid "Generates configuration files for the build"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]build-iso\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:81
msgid ""
"Creates the final ISO image, incorporating both the core SquashFS image and "
"any additional modules"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]remove-sources\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:84
msgid "Removes source files after the build"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: minios-live.1:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "USAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]start_cmd\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:89
msgid ""
"(Optional) The build stage to start from.  If omitted, starts from the first "
"command"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]-\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:92
msgid "(Optional) A range operator for running command sequences"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: minios-live.1:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\f[B]end_cmd\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:96
msgid ""
"(Optional) The build stage to end with.  If omitted, ends with the last "
"command"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: minios-live.1:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:99
msgid "\\f[B]No arguments (./minios-live)\\f[R]: Displays help information\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:101
msgid "\\f[B]Single command\\f[R]: Runs only that specific command\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:104
msgid ""
"\\f[B]start_cmd - end_cmd\\f[R]: Runs all commands from start_cmd to "
"end_cmd\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:106
msgid "\\f[B]- end_cmd\\f[R]: Runs from the beginning up to end_cmd\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:108
msgid "\\f[B]start_cmd -\\f[R]: Runs from start_cmd to completion\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:110
msgid ""
"\\f[B]- only\\f[R]: Runs the entire build process from start to finish\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: minios-live.1:110 minios-cmd.1:153 condinapt.1:293 condinapt-minios.7:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:112
msgid "Run the build from start to finish:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "minios-live -\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:119
msgid ""
"Start the build by building the base environment and finish by installing "
"the entire system in chroot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "minios-live build-bootstrap - build-chroot\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:126
msgid ""
"Start the build from the beginning and finish by installing the entire "
"system in chroot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "minios-live - build-chroot\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:132
msgid "Start the build by building the base environment and run to completion:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "minios-live build-bootstrap -\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:138
msgid "Build only ISO image from previously prepared data:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "minios-live build-iso\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: minios-live.1:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:148
msgid ""
"Edit the configuration file \\f[B]/etc/minios-live/build.conf\\f[R] to "
"specify your preferred distribution, desktop environment, and additional "
"software to be included in the SquashFS modules.  Alternatively, use "
"\\f[B]minios-cmd\\f[R](1) for an easier configuration experience.\\fR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: minios-live.1:154
msgid ""
"This modular approach allows for greater flexibility and maintainability "
"when customizing your MiniOS live system.  You can easily add or update "
"software by modifying the SquashFS module configurations and rebuilding only "
"the affected modules using the appropriate \\f[B]minios-live\\f[R] command."
"\\fR"
msgstr ""

